      "content": "Examining the transcript carefully will help. Pay close attention to the context of his responses. If there was sufficient detail in his answers that directly addressed the questions without infringing on classified information, his explanation could stand as a legitimate legal protection. On the other hand, repeated evasion or vague answers that seem designed to obscure the answer could indeed be construed as a deliberate attempt to mislead the committee. The key is whether the questions were answered with factual clarity while respecting the classified information, not just an apparent attempt at evasion without substance. Assess how well the high-ranking official balanced transparency with confidentiality obligations during his testimony.",
